From a4d4667508f1dab70f77d89df881374b02829c3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Antonio Borneo <antonio.borneo@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 2 Jun 2026 17:37:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] bus: stm32_firewall: reduce the verbosity for not accessible
 peripherals

Depending on security settings of the platform, some peripheral
can be not accessible.

Don't log an error message in this case; use a debug message.

Signed-off-by: Antonio Borneo <antonio.borneo@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I1b74acb0123ab1d000bcc84aad6bb1e080e4c0d2
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/573870
Reviewed-by: Amelie DELAUNAY <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Domain-Review: Amelie DELAUNAY <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
---
 drivers/bus/stm32_firewall.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/bus/stm32_firewall.c
+++ b/drivers/bus/stm32_firewall.c
@@ -326,7 +326,7 @@ int stm32_firewall_populate_bus(struct s
 				 */
 				fwnode_links_purge(of_fwnode_handle(child));
 				of_detach_node(child);
-				dev_err(parent, "%s: Device driver will not be probed\n",
+				dev_dbg(parent, "%s: Device driver will not be probed\n",
 					child->full_name);
 			}
 		}
